<title>GREECE: IONIAN BANK LOWERS TIME DEPOSIT RATES.</title>
<headline>IONIAN BANK LOWERS TIME DEPOSIT RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Ionian Bank said</p>
<p>on Wednesday it is lowering its time deposit rates by 50 basis</p>
<p>points effective Thursday September 26.</p>
<p>Time Deposits (from 500,000 to 25 mln drachmas)</p>
<p>Three months  12.00 from 12.50 percent</p>
<p>    Six months    12.25 from 12.75 percent</p>
<p>    Nine months   12.25 from 12.75 percent</p>
<p>    One year	12.50 from 13.00 percent</p>
<p>For amounts over 25 million drachmas the deposit rate is</p>
<p>negotiable, it said.</p>
<p>Certificates of Deposit as per decree 109/87 ( from five to</p>
<p>25 mln drachmas)</p>
<p>Three months  12.00 from 12.50 percent</p>
<p>    Six months    12.25 from 12.75 percent</p>
<p>    One year	12.50 from 13.00 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
